/target
# Everything in models/ is local (weights, symlinks, dialect/template
# sidecars) except the README and the sampling sidecars: those are what
# blallama actually serves with, so they are versioned — a diff shows a
# missing id_patterns block before an agent cohort runs without it.
# `model.sampling.toml` stays local: `model.gguf` is a per-machine link
# (a different quant on each box), and the model tests load through it.
# Backups (`*.sampling.toml.bak*`) do not match and stay local.
# Canonical patched templates live versioned under
# tests/fixtures/templates/.
models/*
!models/README.md
!models/*.sampling.toml
models/model.sampling.toml
/Cargo.lock
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
model.sampling.toml
/profile.py
/bench.py
/prefill_prompt.txt
/__pycache__/
/fuzz-corpus/
/prefill_prompt_long.txt
screenshots/
.claude/docs/*.pdf
.DS_Store

# Default output dir of `council --dump` (exit-interview transcripts)
/council_prompts/
